// The same response with one declared field answered outside its coproduct: extdeps.github.github::
// UserType's arms are User, Bot, Organization. This is what a refusal of a real pull-request read looks
// like, so the refusal line is checked against a body a person can read.
data pull_16122_response_with_unestablished_author: String = "{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/gunb-ai/gunbc/pulls/16122\",\"id\":5216318918,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDORCvEH88AAAABNuq1xg\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/pull/16122\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/pull/16122.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/pull/16122.patch\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/gunb-ai/gunbc/issues/16122\",\"commits_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/gunb-ai/gunbc/pulls/16122/commits\",\"review_comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/gunb-ai/gunbc/pulls/16122/comments\",\"review_comment_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/gunb-ai/gunbc/pulls/comments{/number}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/gunb-ai/gunbc/issues/16122/comments\",\"statuses_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/gunb-ai/gunbc/statuses/75355151e3ac5d0222d0d919d54ac8cf196b9002\",\"number\":16122,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"equality admission: one authority for the equality-admissible set; the three refused sites return to structural '=='\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"gunbai-bot[bot]\",\"id\":289086189,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOETsa7Q\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/3909950?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gunbai-bot%5Bbot%5D\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/gunbai-bot\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gunbai-bot%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gunbai-bot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gunbai-bot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gunbai-bot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gunbai-bot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gunbai-bot%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gunbai-bot%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gunbai-bot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gunbai-bot%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\"type\":\"Human\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"body\":\"## What this lands\\n\\nOne rule decides whether a type argument may use structural `==`: `v1.compiler.infer::equality_argument_by_target`. Main's positional rule is kept — every type **argument written at an applied reference** is judged, because a derived Rust impl bounds every parameter — and the rule gains the two cases it was missing:\\n\\n- **`equality_argument_is_enclosing_type_parameter`** — an argument that is a type parameter of the declaration the walk is inside. The roster rides in `InferScope.enclosing_declared_type_param_names`, filled by `equality_scope_with_params` when the walk enters a declaration's own members.\\n- **`is_unit_variant_phantom_argument`** — a unit-variant marker used as a type argument (`Length`, `RackUnitHeight` in `Measure<Length, RackUnitHeight, Nat>`), through the resolver's own lookup `v1.compiler.infer_env::lookup_unit_variant_phantom_type`. No new authority.\\n\\nBoth stay **after** `expand_nominal_alias_rhs`, where they shipped. An earlier commit on this branch (`44c956632168`) moved them ahead of that step on the reading that the expansion destroys the spelling the arms ask about; that reading came from a build that had not recompiled the partition crates, and it is reverted — see *Two withdrawn reads* below.\\n\\nThe three refused sites go back to plain `==`: `host_effect_is_converge_loop_evidence`, `seat_fell_by`, `fleet_nominal_rackmount_arithmetic_holds`. The `measure_count` cardinality rewrites and the hand-written constructor match go with them, imports included — the old answers end in one motion at their root.\\n\\nSeed: `src/v1/04_infer.dag` **+89 / −3**. The growth replaces three per-site workarounds that were inline at the call sites; no scaffold file is removed because none existed.\\n\\n## Controls\\n\\nMeasured with a compiler built from this branch's seed and mirror at `eeae4193aaf5`, **with the partition crates recompiled**.\\n\\n| control | result |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `dag/gunbc/host/host_effect.dag` resolve | PASS — `NoSuchFunction` for the empty name, **zero equality rows**, zero resolve-failed, 825 modules, 5.28 GiB |\\n| `dag/gunbc/compute/compute_seat_ensure.dag` resolve | PASS — zero equality rows, 1042 modules, 6.96 GiB, no OOM |\\n| `dag/gunbc/fleet/fleet_physical_inventory.dag` resolve | PASS — zero equality rows, 168 modules, 0.64 GiB |\\n| the same three at `3d34fc61ca6e`, before the rule existed | RED at `host_effect_is_converge_loop_evidence`, `seat_fell_by`, `fleet_nominal_rackmount_arithmetic_holds` |\\n| witness module, `claim_batch --wet`, all 80 controls | **76 PASS / 4 FAIL**, 6 min, zero equality-admission rows. The four failures are the optional/`Present` controls; they fail identically under a compiler built from `origin/main` and belong to #16206 |\\n| `nested_structural_argument_equality_admits_at_the_use` | PASS — the use site that used to refuse now admits; the permanent green control |\\n| `an_unresolved_type_name_still_refuses_blocking` | PASS — a name the reading could not bind still refuses; the repair does not admit \\\"any unresolved name\\\" |\\n| `a_function_typed_argument_refuses_even_in_a_phantom_position` | PASS — `Engine<Value>`-shaped arguments still refuse; this is what kept the E0369 class out |\\n| control 3c, `gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:self-host` | `exit_status=0 warning_count=0 wall_s=824`, **zero E0369, zero E0277**, emitted closure `d4d72cb053f9…` — the closure that failed v2-bootstrap 42414168425 with E0369 builds under rustc |\\n| `dag/gunbc/integration_concern.dag` resolve | PASS with the ledger rewritten, 0.58 GiB |\\n\\n## Two withdrawn reads, and the build defect behind both\\n\\nThe generated mirrors under `src/v1/stage0/src/` are pulled into the **partition** crates (`src/v1/stage0_v1_infer`, `stage0_emit_core`, `stage0_std_surface`, …) through `#[path]` includes that live outside those crates' own `src/`. `cargo build --release -p v1-compiler` does **not** recompile them when only mirrors change — it finishes in ~23 s and the binary keeps the rule compiled earlier. Correct local procedure: `touch src/v1/<partition>/src/lib.rs` (or build `--workspace`) before building. CI is unaffected; it builds the workspace.\\n\\nTwo reads on this PR were produced that way and are withdrawn:\\n\\n1. the AFTER runs reported at `e810fb31514f` (green against a stale rule), and\\n2. the claim in `44c956632168` that with the arms after `expand_nominal_alias_rhs`, `Holder<FooBarUnit>` on a marker declared in the specimen module, `Holder<RackUnitHeight>`, `Holder<Length>`, `Pair<Length, Nat>` and the written `Measure<Length, RackUnitHeight, Nat>` refused. With the crates recompiled, the arms in the position they ship admit every one of those specimens, and the three entries pass. The reordering changed nothing measurable, so it is reverted (`8522ae255791`): an unjustified change to a load-bearing stage does not belong here.\\n\\nWhat is left measured in the corrected build: the direct spellings admit, and the alias spellings refuse — which is the gap recorded below, not a property of the arm order.\\n\\n## Recorded, not folded in\\n\\nNew row `equality_alias_argument_not_expanded_before_admission` (Open, rostered in `integration_concerns`): an argument written **through a nominal alias** refuses while the same type spelled as an application admits — in one specimen module `Holder<Measure<Length, RackUnitHeight, Nat>>` and `Box<Measure<…>>` admit, `Holder<RackUnit>`, `Box<RackUnit>` and `Holder<MyUnit>` (the alias declared in that module) refuse. `expand_nominal_alias_rhs` returns the right-hand side under `with_authored_identity`, so the recurse guard sees neither an identity change nor a connective change and the arm falls through to refusal. Admission stricter than emission, fail-closed, and nothing in the three-site wall depends on it — the three sites write the application directly. The row carries the specimens and the next rung.\\n\\n## Ledger\\n\\n`equality_wall_three_site_measure_stopgap_interim` closes as `Integrated` at `eeae4193aaf5` — the revision where the seed and the published mirror that make the three entries admit are both present — with the superseded stopgaps cited at the revisions that introduced them (`f9bad88f8a56` for #16099, `3ca4fe166b5d` for #16045), the replacement cited as `equality_argument_by_target` plus the two arms, and five retained executions. Per review 92792 the row's `question` is now the historical question in past tense: the present-tense sentences that contradicted the disposition (\\\"what this row carries is the record that they are interim\\\", the duplicated-constructor-shape sentence about a match this PR deletes, and \\\"#15992 itself remains blocked … the wall and its interim both stay open\\\") are gone. `host_effect_apply_witness_import_block_absent` keeps its own `Open` disposition on its own row.\\n\\n## Stage0 mirror\\n\\n`src/v1/stage0/src/*.rs` are generated (`// Generated by v1 compiler -- do not edit.`). This branch does not hand-edit them: heal regenerates them from the seed and publishes the commit, and v2-bootstrap judges the published mirror.\\n\\n## Merge\\n\\nNot merged here. I will ask the operator to land it once CI is green on the merged head and the tally is met.\\n\",\"labels\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-11-08T23:38:04Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-11-10T09:02:10Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"merged_at\":null,\"merge_commit_sha\":\"ae10859313035c60a47726eea8c52251cdfbbca0\",\"assignee\":null,\"assignees\":[],\"requested_reviewers\":[],\"requested_teams\":[],\"head\":{\"label\":\"gunb-ai:equality-admission-repair\",\"ref\":\"equality-admission-repair\",\"repo\":{\"id\":1143718943,\"node_id\":\"R_kgDORCvEHw\",\"name\":\"gunbc\",\"full_name\":\"gunb-ai/gunbc\",\"owner\":{\"login\":\"gunb-ai\",\"id\":244123794,\"node_id\":\"O_kgDODo0Ikg\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244123794?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gunb-ai\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/gunb-ai\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gunb-ai/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gunb-ai/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gunb-ai/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gunb-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gunb-ai/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gunb-ai/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gunb-ai/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gunb-ai/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gunb-ai/received_events\",\"type\":\"Organization\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"private\":false,\"fork\":false,\"archived\":false,\"disabled\":false,\"description\":\"Home of the Daglang compiler\",\"homepage\":\"https://gunb.ai\",\"language\":\"Rust\",\"visibility\":\"public\",\"is_template\":false,\"topics\":[],\"forks_count\":0,\"forks\":0,\"stargazers_count\":4,\"watchers_count\":4,\"watchers\":4,\"open_issues_count\":119,\"open_issues\":119,\"size\":762021,\"default_branch\":\"main\",\"has_issues\":true,\"has_projects\":true,\"has_wiki\":true,\"has_pages\":false,\"has_downloads\":false,\"has_discussions\":false,\"has_pull_requests\":true,\"pushed_at\":\"2026-11-10T10:44:26Z\",\"created_at\":\"2026-01-27T23:04:32Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-11-10T09:34:59Z\",\"allow_forking\":true,\"web_commit_signoff_required\":false,\"pull_request_creation_policy\":\"all\",\"license\":{\"key\":\"other\",\"name\":\"Other\",\"url\":null,\"spdx_id\":\"NOASSERTION\",\"node_id\":\"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA=\"},\"url\":\"htt